 with a $1.2B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +20% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $200M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +11.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +11.7% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 51% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Forestar Group (FOR) Could Be 27% Below Fair Value Following Weaker Earnings And Board Changes","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate-management-and-development/nyse-for/forestar-group/news/forestar-group-for-could-be-27-below-fair-value-following-we","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793875528.463,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"FOR Q3 deep dive: weaker demand, margin pressures, and cautious outlook for land development","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/q3-deep-dive-weaker-demand-232536848.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793661936.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.586,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Forestar Group COO Mark Walker Vests 3,607 RSUs and Surrenders Shares for Taxes on October 29, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/forestar-group-coo-mark-walker-vests-3607-rsus-and-surrenders-shares-for-taxes-on-october-29-2026","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793659845.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Forestar Group CEO Anthony W. Oxley Vests 6,319 RSUs and Surrenders Shares for Tax on October 29, 2026","