e another (dispersion 10%).","On multiples it looks cheap against Real Estate peers: P/E 8.5 vs 23.6 and EV/EBITDA 7.9 vs 16.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 24% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of -16.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 15.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 2 covering analysts target $34.00 on average, 43% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 11% earns above the cost of capital of 7.8%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.39).","It burns cash (FCF margin -12%).","Earnings quality is a concern: a weak Piotroski score of 1/9, cash conversion of only -1.18x and high accruals (+11.7% of assets).","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is -12%.","ROE of 9% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.4% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.9x net debt to EBITDA ($379.2M of cash against $802.7M of debt), above the 1.5x gate.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.76 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 3.1% over 3 years, 12.3% over 5 years and 20.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 81%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 74%.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (0.1% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is -0, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and institutions hold 38%.","The share count has grown 0.6% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["CEO pay is $1.9M."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":70,"head":"Invest: trades 44% below fair va